  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that PCA-based RNA multiprofile with avgpool improves substantially over singleprofile PCA. The key uncertainty is whether the gain is specific to avgpool or whether a transformer aggregation can further improve multiprofile RNA representations. config_003 tests this by changing only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping model setting, profile setting, and RNA encoder fixed. This is the best next use of budget because it exploits the current promising direction while cleanly isolating the effect of aggregation before moving to more complex image or multimodal designs."
